    "status": "draft",
    "review": {
      "reviewer": "Tim Validasi SIGRAK",
      "status": "pending",
      "rule": "D-113: nothing here is imported or seeded before Tim Validasi SIGRAK signs it off."
    },
    "source_ref": "docs/sources/usulan-01/data/pilihan-isian.json",
    "source_sha256": "86f7d97ecd0a0e639838df34a9c5ad2c7a2211fbf71ec53b1cffcfafbeedd00d",
    "converted_on": "2026-11-09",
    "decisions": {
      "D-029": "Attendance is daily and recorded by the homeroom teacher.",
      "D-036": "Non-cognitive diagnostic answers never go to the AI.",
      "D-214": "A2 diagnostic assessment and the H1 Fase A rapor without numbers are in scope.",
      "D-304": "Mutasi is saved as a draft until it is set.",
      "D-305": "Only the SIGRAK labels reach the UI; legacy labels stay as reference (legacy_label).",
      "D-367": "Curated with SIGRAK names, keys, and codes."
    },
    "conventions": [
      "Keys are English snake_case and never change once seeded; labels and other text shown to users are Indonesian.",
      "Codes follow SIGRAK-KAT-<AREA>-NN for the main items of a file and SIGRAK-KAT-<AREA>-<LIST>-NN for its secondary lists (see README.md). Codes are stable: a retired item keeps its code, and new items take the next free number.",
      "No identifier from the legacy app is carried over. Where a decision keeps an old label for reference (D-305), it sits in legacy_label and is never shown in the UI.",
      "review_notes are Indonesian notes for Tim Validasi SIGRAK; they are not shown to teachers.",
      "groups bundle the fields and option lists of one form. A list has a code SIGRAK-KAT-OPS-<LIST>; each option has SIGRAK-KAT-OPS-<LIST>-NN.",
      "fields describe free-entry inputs (type: text, date, time, student, option, rupiah, rupiah_computed); they have keys but no codes.",
      "Keys match the data model where a column exists: attendance_records.status, student_notes.kind, report_cards.numeric_grades."
    ]
  },
